       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen.\n\n- **Order as written:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum for adults:** The prescribing maximum is 3200 mg/day for prescription use, and usually no more than 800 mg in a single dose. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't make it safe.\n\nThe dose may have been a typo, for example 1600 mg/day or 400 mg four times daily. Here are some common regimens:\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that you intend something different and give me the clinical reason. I'll enter it once the dose is clarified."
