       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and 6400 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum. I don't know of any standard adult protocol that uses that dose. The closest is high-dose ibuprofen for cystic fibrosis, which is dosed differently and guided by drug levels. Because the potential harm is serious (GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events), I'd rather not enter it on an unverified statement.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within labeled limits.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day) or 600 mg PO every 6 hours. I can enter either now.\n- **Enter the high-dose order through your hospital's override process.** If a protocol exists, the pharmacy or attending can place the order with the protocol referenced. Pharmacy may need to verify it, and I can't substitute for that.\n- **Add a note.** If you'd like, I can enter a labeled-limit dose with a note saying that a higher-dose protocol is being verified with pharmacy.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
